  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: The largest single-variable gain so far came from upgrading the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (+4 pts, config_019→config_031), while the image encoder choice (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) showed negligible difference (0.639 vs 0.635). Question: Does a more sophisticated RNA encoder (scgpt) continue to improve performance beyond scvi_n200, or does the RNA-encoder axis plateau? config_043 changes only the RNA encoder from the current best (config_031: scvi_n200→scgpt), keeping all other settings (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) fixed. Why best next: It directly tests whether the RNA-encoder trend continues, which is the highest-leverage remaining design question. A positive result opens a new exploitation path (scgpt + vit_l, etc.); a null result confirms scvi_n200 is near-optimal and redirects effort to other dimensions. Under a limited budget, resolving the RNA-encoder ceiling is more informative than re-testing the already-near-resolved image-encoder choice."
}

